LiquidLaneRedeemCapability
├── implementation installation and replacement
│   ├── rejects invalid Reactor or protocol
│   ├── preserves signatures and adapter storage on compatible replacement
│   └── different Reactor rejects old signatures but can revoke through their original Reactor
├── signRequest
│   ├── requires a Merkle-authorized adapter self-call
│   ├── rejects zero input, expiry, empty signatures, and invalid outputs
│   ├── binds protocol and every output recipient to the adapter
│   ├── rejects active token/nonce conflicts and consumed Reactor nonces
│   └── signs without touching balances or allowances, including without funding
├── isValidSignature
│   ├── rejects absent, empty, mismatched, expired, revoked, and consumed signatures
│   ├── binds every request field to the upstream Reactor digest
│   └── rejects a different chain, Reactor, or storage context
├── Reactor fill through LiquidLaneAdapter
│   ├── spends adapter tokens using separately authorized approve actions
│   ├── delivers every output to the adapter
│   └── rolls back nonce and transfers on failed settlement
├── revokeRequest and finalizeRequest
│   ├── require authorized self-calls and known requests
│   ├── revoke signature and invalidate original Reactor nonce
│   ├── finalize only filled, revoked, or expired requests
│   └── never transfer tokens or change allowances, even with paused tokens
└── removal
    ├── may leave outstanding requests and approvals
    └── compatible reinstallation restores stored unexpired signatures
